=== p2-windows · W7 · page:analytics/PeriodCompare (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:analytics/PeriodCompare   kind=page   web route=/period-compare
Web source  : web/src/features/analytics/pages/PeriodComparePage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  TimelinePage / TrueCostPage / WeeklyDigestPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "PeriodComparePage.xaml +
  PeriodComparePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Analytics" is mapped onto these real conventions (the
  project is TeslaSync.App, not TeslaSync); the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name
  ("PeriodCompare", already in RouteTable.cs → /period-compare) in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useVehicles (GET /vehicles); the page additionally derives
  every panel from the two GET /analytics/period-stats queries (one per period) the web page runs via useQuery +
  request(). The view-model reads all three through an injected IPeriodCompareFeed; the default
  EmptyPeriodCompareFeed resolves the empty state (matching the sibling host-injection precedent), and the
  generated-client-backed PeriodCompareClientFeed (PeriodComparePage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI
  contract operations get_api_v1_vehicles (no params) + get_api_v1_analytics_period_stats (snake_case vehicle_id +
  days query params, never camelCase, never a double /api/v1 prefix), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. No
  HTTP touches the view; non-success surfaces as an exception -> the failure banner.
- The web page renders the disambiguation banner (multi-vehicle accounts only) + the selectors GlassPanel always,
  the failure banner (PageContainer error) above the gated body, a Skeleton while the first load is in flight and
  an EmptyState when !a||!b; the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent regions per ADR-006: selectors
  GlassPanel always visible; loading -> TsPageLoadSkeleton; empty -> TsEmptyState (web compare.empty); error ->
  TsAlertBanner(Danger); success -> the six metric cards + the side-by-side TsBarChart (in a TsChartContainer) +
  the comparison table (per-row TsBadge for % change) + the insights. Never a blank region.
- SI units (ADR P1/S5): GET /analytics/period-stats returns display units (km, kWh, Wh/km, kg). Distance and
  efficiency are restated to the user's UnitPref at the projection boundary only — distance via
  UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi(total_distance_km * 1000, pref.Distance), efficiency * 1.609344 for mi (web
  convertDistanceFromSI + avg_efficiency * KM_PER_MILE) — and every number is formatted through the shared
  NumberFormatting port (web fmtNumber default precision 2; the % change at precision 1), verified by
  Metrics_convert_distance_and_efficiency_to_imperial_units. No non-SI value is ever stored or computed.
- i18n: all 34 manifest keys already existed in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (translation.compare.*); the
  surface resolves every visible literal through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names + the English
  defaults verbatim. No catalog edits were needed.
- Tests link the three Microsoft.UI-free files (Model/Source/ViewModel) into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj via the
  established <Compile Include … Link="FeatureViews\PeriodComparePage\…"> convention (the headless test assembly
  cannot reference the WinUI exe); the bare WinUI view (PeriodComparePage.cs) is excluded (it uses Microsoft.UI).

